cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the release you used (its git tag and Zenodo DOI)."
title: "Bitcoin Data Labs L2 Audit Dataset: Liquid Network custody, reserves, peg flows and incidents"
type: dataset
version: "v2026.11.18"
date-released: 2026-11-18
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Saurabh
    affiliation: Bitcoin Data Labs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7944-3492"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bitcoindatalabs/l2-data"
url: "https://bitcoindatalabs.org"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A reproducible audit of Bitcoin layer-2 systems from public chain data, starting with the Liquid Network:
  every Bitcoin output that has held Liquid reserves since 2018, the reserve against L-BTC outstanding at every
  Bitcoin block, every peg-in and peg-out with both legs and the delay between them, the federation's spending
  paths and timelocks, block production, and incidents found by fixed rules. Release v0.1 runs to Bitcoin block
  976,206 (2026-11-17) and Liquid block 4,148,532.
keywords:
  - Bitcoin
  - Liquid Network
  - Sidechain
  - Proof of reserves
  - Federated peg
  - Layer 2
  - Bitcoin Data Labs
